[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: System Requirements Specification - IRONAIR
UID: DOC-SRS001
VERSION: 1.1.0
OPTIONS:
  MARKUP: Text

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SRS-PURPOSE
TITLE: Purpose, sources, and software boundary

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This System Requirements Specification (SRS) defines the iron-air-modeling plant
that the ironair Python package SHALL simulate. Physical architecture, chemistry,
electrolyte, air-electrode, iron-electrode, vessel, and grid-storage operating
envelopes are derived from two Form Energy disclosures:

- US12308414B2, Device architectures for metal-air batteries (granted 2025-05-20;
  Appl. 16/913,877; published family WO2020264344A1 / EP3991234A1 / CN114207915A).
- EP4602674A1, Electrode configurations for iron-air electrochemical systems
  (published 2025-08-20; Appl. EP23878232.0; WO2024081792A1; priority US 63/379,223).

The patents overlap as a dual-electrode iron-air family: separate oxygen reduction
reaction (ORR) and oxygen evolution reaction (OER) positives, an iron-containing
negative, and alkaline aqueous electrolyte. US12308414B2 emphasizes vessel,
submerged/stacked ORR, air delivery, and DRI-pellet anodes. EP4602674A1 emphasizes
channeled/interdigitated iron and OER electrodes for thick, high-areal-capacity
anodes. Where they differ, both configurations SHALL be modelable.
<<<

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The software is an installable Python package that reconstructs the patented plant
as coupled ODE/DAE components. Passing tests verifies the software against this
SRS; it does not constitute experimental hardware validation of US12308414B2 or
EP4602674A1.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Python package
STATEMENT: >>>
The software SHALL be implemented as an installable Python package named ironair.

All public APIs SHALL be importable using:

  import ironair
  from ironair import constants
  from ironair import chemistry
  from ironair import components
  from ironair import simulation
  from ironair import scenarios
  from ironair import plotting

The implementation SHALL use a standard src/ package layout.

The project SHALL provide editable installation using:

  pip install -e ".[dev,notebooks]"
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A single installable package is the integration boundary for notebooks, tests, and
coupled simulation of the patented iron-air plant. The SDRS src/ layout takes
precedence over the generic no-src-directory Cursor rule for this project.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Package ironair installs in a virtual environment. The listed imports succeed after
pip install -e ".[dev,notebooks]" or the equivalent uv installation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-006
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Patent-grounded plant of record
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulated plant of record SHALL be a rechargeable aqueous alkaline iron-air
battery with a dual-electrode air side (distinct ORR discharge cathode and OER
charge cathode), an iron-containing metal electrode, and a liquid electrolyte that
separates the air-side electrodes from the metal electrode.

The plant SHALL be consistent with US12308414B2 Claim 1 (ORR, OER, metal electrode,
and electrolyte) and with EP4602674A1 Claim 1 (iron electrode, ORR electrode with
air-facing surface, interdigitated OER, and contacting electrolyte).

Primary-only (ORR-only air electrode) operation MAY be enabled as a documented
reduced-order mode but SHALL be identified as non-rechargeable relative to the
secondary dual-electrode plant.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Summary and FIG. 1A define metal-air cells with anode, cathode,
electrolyte, and optional gaseous headspace. EP4602674A1 [0048]-[0049] and FIG. 1
define dual-electrode iron-air cells with switchable charge (OER) and discharge
(ORR) paths.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Family note: US12308414B2 is the granted US member of WO2020264344. EP4602674A1 is
the EP publication of WO2024081792 and is not a literal equivalent of US12308414B2;
it is a later electrode-geometry disclosure in the same iron-air product family.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SRS-MISSION
TITLE: Mission, duration, and grid context

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Both patents frame iron-air cells as long-duration and ultra-long-duration energy
storage (LODES) for electric power grids. US12308414B2 Background states that
existing storage covers milliseconds to hours and that systems of at least 8 h are
needed. The detailed description defines long/ultra-long duration as 8 h or longer,
including 8-20 h, 20-24 h, a week, and seasonal (days to months to a year) storage
of surplus solar generation. EP4602674A1 [0002] restates the greater-than-8 h need.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-007
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Long-duration energy storage mission
STATEMENT: >>>
The system SHALL model grid-connected LODES operation with energy storage durations
of 8 hours or longer, including 8 h, 8-20 h, 20 h, 20-24 h, 24 h, week-scale, and
seasonal (multi-day to multi-month) windows as defined in US12308414B2 (long
duration / ultra-long duration; LODES).

Anode thickness and independent charge versus discharge length scales SHALL be
parameterizable so that example durations disclosed in US12308414B2 can be
represented: about 3-5 cm anode thickness for about 100 h; about 4-6 cm for about
300 h; and an asymmetric example of about 100 h charge with about 300 h discharge
for a 5 cm by 5 cm square anode cross-section.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Definitions and Detailed Description (anode thickness versus duration;
symmetric versus asymmetric duration). EP4602674A1 [0002] and [0045] motivate thick
high-areal-capacity iron electrodes to amortize air-electrode cost.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Default demonstration discharge of 100 h (3.6e5 s) is the short end of the patented
LODES range, not a claim that hardware has been validated at that duration.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Integrated physics simulation
STATEMENT: >>>
The software SHALL model the complete iron-air battery as a coupled multiphysics
system corresponding to the patented plant.

The model SHALL include metallic iron electrode, iron hydroxide and oxide phases,
oxygen reduction electrode, oxygen evolution electrode, hydrogen evolution,
alkaline electrolyte, electrolyte transport, separator, gas diffusion layer,
current collectors, cell assembly, thermal system, air intake, fan/blower, gas
manifolds, ventilation, electrolyte reservoir, circulation pump, piping, valves,
heat exchanger, battery stack, battery module, battery enclosure, DC electrical
distribution, DC/DC conversion, grid inverter, transformer, grid interface,
and degradation and aging.

Measurement sensors, dedicated supervisory-controller classes, fault-management
modules, and state estimators SHALL remain design allocations until implemented
(IA-FLT-001, IA-CTL-001, IA-EST-001). Discrete charge/discharge/rest modes SHALL
be provided by plant_sim.plant.PlantModel.

These components SHALL interact through shared physical quantities and conserved
material, charge, and energy flows.

Vessel, lid, and air-delivery functions disclosed in US12308414B2 (electrolyte
containment, secondary containment, thermal management cavity, air distribution,
process-gas venting, current collection, sensing, DC connections) SHALL map onto
the enclosure, air-system, thermal, collector, and control components listed
above.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Balance-of-plant and grid interfaces determine operating envelopes of the
electrochemical cell. US12308414B2 FIGS. 1E-1F, 9A, and 94-102 describe
multi-function vessels, lids, and bulk energy storage systems. EP4602674A1 FIG. 1
adds the dual-electrode switch between power source (charge) and load (discharge).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Changed because ironair.components is empty and CoupledSystem does not assemble the
patented plant. plant_sim.plant.PlantModel concatenates the implemented component
RHS functions. Sensors and estimators are not in that concatenation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-008
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Dual-electrode charge and discharge paths
STATEMENT: >>>
During charge the model SHALL electrically connect the iron electrode to the OER
electrode and a power source so that iron species are reduced toward metallic
Fe(0).

During discharge the model SHALL electrically connect the iron electrode to the
ORR electrode and a load so that metallic iron is oxidized toward higher-valence
species including Fe(OH)2 and Fe3O4.

A mode switch SHALL select charge versus discharge electrical paths as in
EP4602674A1 [0049] switch 116 and US12308414B2 FIGS. 5A-5B toggle switch 550.

OER and ORR electrodes SHALL be allowed to be electrically separated so that the
ORR electrode is not exposed to high OER operating potentials that can damage or
oxidize the ORR electrode (US12308414B2 FIGS. 5A-5B).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
EP4602674A1 [0048]-[0049] and US12308414B2 dual-cathode architecture. Independent
OER/ORR materials and geometries are separately optimized (US12308414B2).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The supervisory controller implements the switch as a discrete operating mode, not
as a hidden mutation of plant parameters.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SRS-US-ARCH
TITLE: US12308414B2 device architecture (granted claims)

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
US12308414B2 Claim 1 is the granted independent claim: a battery with ORR electrode,
OER electrode, metal electrode, and electrolyte separating the air-side electrodes
from the metal electrode, wherein the ORR electrode is submerged, comprises a
series of discrete ORR sections stacked vertically below the electrolyte surface,
each section geometry varies with depth, and pressure drop across each stacked
section is the same in the depth direction. Claims 2-18 add dual electrodes,
stackable vessels, wavy/rippled ORR, can-negative housing, inverse-air frames and
boxes, supplied air, curved/tube ORR, movable metal electrode, airflow ramps,
airflow-flex electrical separation, porous ORR separator, and DRI pellet beds.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-009
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Submerged stacked ORR with depth-equalized pressure drop
STATEMENT: >>>
The system SHALL support a submerged ORR electrode comprising a series of discrete
ORR electrode sections arranged vertically in a stack below the electrolyte
surface.

Each discrete ORR section SHALL have geometry that can vary with depth below the
electrolyte surface.

The air-path model SHALL be able to impose equal pressure drop across each stacked
ORR section in the depth direction.

This configuration SHALL be the default representation of US12308414B2 Claim 1.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Claim 1. Detailed description FIGS. 25A-36B, 57-58, and 35A-35C
describe stacked-core / distillation-column ORR layers with depth-dependent bubble
thickness, baffles, and cascading air.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Equal pressure drop is an algebraic hydraulic constitutive law, not an artificial
dynamic lag (IA-SYS-003).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-010
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Separate ORR and OER electrodes
STATEMENT: >>>
The system SHALL model ORR and OER as separate electrodes (US12308414B2 Claim 2)
and SHALL also support a documented bifunctional single air electrode in which ORR
and OER are portions of the same electrode (US12308414B2 Summary).

When separate, both electrodes MAY be submerged (Claim 6).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Claims 2 and 6; Summary dual-electrode versus bifunctional options.
EP4602674A1 uses the dual-electrode configuration as the baseline plant (FIG. 1).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-011
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Stackable vessel and secondary containment
STATEMENT: >>>
The enclosure model SHALL represent a stackable vessel that supports ORR, OER,
metal electrode, and electrolyte and is configured to self-stack on other vessels
(US12308414B2 Claim 3).

The vessel SHALL be modelable as a double-walled container with an inner wall
(primary electrolyte vessel), outer wall (secondary containment), and cavity used
for thermal-management fluid, electrical isolation, thermal mass, or temporary
electrolyte hold during maintenance (US12308414B2 FIGS. 1E-1F).

A bag-in-box vessel (structural box plus electrolyte bag) SHALL be an allowed
reduced-order containment option.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Claim 3 and vessel description. Self-stacking increases plant power
density (MW/acre). Conductive contact points allow stacked cells in series.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-012
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ORR geometry and inverse air-breathing options
STATEMENT: >>>
The ORR component SHALL support the following patented geometries as selectable
configurations, each identified in metadata:

- wavy or rippled ORR to increase triple-phase boundary at a given footprint
  (US12308414B2 Claim 4; FIGS. 10A-10C);
- frame that displaces electrolyte to create a gas volume at depth (Claim 7);
- box configuration filled with air (Claim 8; FIGS. 14-16 inverse air-breathing);
- supplied-air ORR (Claim 9);
- curved ORR (Claim 10);
- frame trapping supplied air in an air chamber bounded by the ORR surface
  (Claim 11);
- tube-shaped ORR, including circular, oval, teardrop, or polygonal tubes
  (Claim 12; FIGS. 20A-23, 59-62);
- floating ORR at the electrolyte free surface with submerged OER (Summary;
  FIGS. 1B-3);
- vertical natural-air-breathing ORR (FIGS. 4A-8);
- convex oxygen-pocket submerged ORR (FIGS. 17-19B);
- open-bottom inverse air-breathing ORR (FIG. 24);
- helical/auger ORR (FIG. 44);
- rectilinear parallel-plate ORR stacks (FIGS. 45-47B);
- coaxial cylindrical ORR core with hexagonal anode/OER tube (FIGS. 27-34).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Claims 4 and 7-12 plus detailed-description architectures. Inverse
air-breathing submerges ORR so leaks remain internal to the cell.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-013
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Can-negative housing and DRI pellet anode
STATEMENT: >>>
The metal electrode SHALL be modelable as a bed of direct reduced iron (DRI)
pellets or marbles (US12308414B2 Claim 18; FIG. 3 packed bed).

A housing-as-current-conductor (can-negative) configuration SHALL be supported in
which the vessel conducts anode current (Claim 5; FIG. 11). Housing materials
SHALL include polymers (polyethylene, HDPE, UHMW, polypropylene) and metals
(nickel, steel, anodized aluminum, nickel-coated steel or aluminum) as parameters.

The metal electrode position relative to ORR and OER SHALL be changeable
(Claim 13; FIG. 52 movable anode).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Claims 5, 13, and 18. DRI beds provide low-cost iron inventory for
LODES. Can-negative stacked housings enable gravity-driven series connections.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-014
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Airflow regulation and ORR separator
STATEMENT: >>>
The air system SHALL include airflow regulation structures (US12308414B2 Claim 14),
including arrays of ramps configured with holes (Claim 15).

The ORR electrode SHALL optionally include a porous separator (Claim 17), with
pore sizes in the 1 micrometer to 1 centimeter range when wrapping stacked-core
ORR columns (FIG. 36A-36B) to retain gas and limit anode contact with oxygen.

OER and ORR SHALL be electrically separable by presence or absence of airflow that
flexes and displaces the ORR electrode (Claim 16).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 Claims 14-17. Porous wrap prevents horizontal bubble escape and
oxygen-induced self-discharge of adjacent metal anodes.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SRS-EP-ARCH
TITLE: EP4602674A1 electrode configurations (published claims)

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
EP4602674A1 addresses thick iron electrodes whose ionic path length otherwise
degrades coulombic and voltage efficiency. Independent claims 1, 20, 38, 55, 70,
and 77 cover channeled iron with interdigitated OER, discrete anode arrays,
discrete cathode arrays, spiral bifilar iron/OER, and pleated iron/OER. Claim 86
covers a method of forming the Claim 1-19 assembly. The disclosure is pending at
the EPO and is treated as design intent for the model, not as a granted US claim
set.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-015
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Channeled iron electrode with interdigitated OER
STATEMENT: >>>
The system SHALL model an iron electrode in contact with an anode current collector
and comprising a plurality of channels; an ORR electrode with a first surface
facing the channels and an opposing second surface in contact with air; an OER
electrode interdigitated with the channels, with at least a portion of the OER
disposed within the channels in a direction perpendicular to the ORR plane; and
electrolyte in contact with the iron electrode, the ORR first surface, the
channels, and the OER electrode.

This configuration SHALL be the default representation of EP4602674A1 Claim 1
(FIG. 2).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
EP4602674A1 Claim 1 and [0051]-[0058]. Channels carry ionic current while denser
ribs carry electronic current, decoupling porosity trade-offs ([0050]).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-016
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Channel and OER projection geometry
STATEMENT: >>>
Channel and OER geometry parameters SHALL include the ranges disclosed in
EP4602674A1:

- channel average length 3 mm to 50 mm perpendicular to the ORR plane, with
  nested examples 15-35 mm, 15-30 mm, and 15-25 mm (Claim 7; [0053]);
- channel average width 1 mm to 40 mm parallel to the ORR plane, with nested
  examples 2-30 mm, 2-20 mm, and 2-15 mm (Claims 7-8; [0054]);
- adjacent-channel center spacing 10 mm to 50 mm, with nested examples 10-30 mm
  and 10-20 mm (Claim 9; [0055]);
- channel shapes independently rectangular prism, cylindrical, pyramidal, or
  trapezoidal prism (Claim 10);
- sloped channels whose width nearest the ORR is 1 percent to 500 percent greater
  than the width farthest from the ORR (Claim 61; FIG. 5);
- OER cathode projections of average length 3 mm to 50 mm from a trunk, with
  nested examples 5-35 mm and 10-30 mm, and width 0.1-20 mm or 0.5-15 mm
  (Claims 3-4; [0064]-[0065]);
- greater than 25 percent of channels occupied by OER, with optional greater than
  40, 50, or 60 percent (Claim 5; [0066]);
- channel fraction about 0.1 to 0.5, example 0.2 to 0.45, defined as
  CW/(CW + RW); example ChanFrac 0.4 with w_rib 5 mm ([0247], FIGS. 25-26);
- iron-to-OER gap 0.1 mm to 5 mm, example 1-4 mm ([0260]).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
EP4602674A1 Claims 3-10 and 61 and paragraphs [0053]-[0066], [0247], [0260].
Simulations in FIGS. 19-26 use 6 M KOH at 303 K, initial rib porosity 0.6, and
loading 4 g Fe/cm2 when comparing planar, channeled, and interdigitated cells.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-015

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-017
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Discrete anodes, discrete OER cathodes, spiral, and pleated layouts
STATEMENT: >>>
The system SHALL support these additional EP4602674A1 independent architectures as
named configurations:

- plurality of anodes separated by channels, electrically communicating, with
  interdigitated OER (Claim 20; FIG. 12);
- plurality of OER cathodes interdigitated with the anode array and electrically
  communicating with each other (Claim 38);
- iron electrode with channels and a plurality of OER cathodes in the channels
  (Claim 55);
- spiral iron electrode and anode current collector with spiral OER at least
  partially bifilar, ORR facing the spiral axis (Claim 70);
- pleated iron electrode and pleated OER with channels between pleats (Claim 77;
  FIG. 17), optionally with OER on both faces of the iron electrode (Claim 80).

Double-sided cells across a shared current collector (Claim 18; FIGS. 6-8) and
paired cells sharing an air channel between ORR backsides (Claim 19; FIGS. 9-11)
SHALL be supported.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
EP4602674A1 independent Claims 20, 38, 55, 70, 77 and dependent Claims 18-19.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-015

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-018
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Iron loading, electrolyte volume fraction, and spine/rib porosity
STATEMENT: >>>
Iron electrode areal loading SHALL be parameterizable from 1 g Fe/cm2 to 7 g Fe/cm2
relative to the direction perpendicular to the ORR electrode (EP4602674A1 Claims 16,
36, 52, 68, 75, 84).

Electrolyte volume fraction in the iron electrode SHALL be parameterizable from
0.5 to 0.9 based on total electrode volume when fully charged (Claims 17, 37, 53,
69, 76, 85), measurable in hardware by mercury porosimetry.

Spine portions connecting ribs MAY have electrolyte volume fraction 2-20 vol%
(example 5-15 vol%) lower than ribs, spine thickness 10-50% of rib thickness, and
spine porosity at least 5 vol% lower than ribs, or alternatively spine and rib
porosity within plus or minus 5% ([0059]-[0061]).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
EP4602674A1 Claims 16-17 and [0059]-[0061]. Higher loading amortizes air-electrode
cost ([0045]) but planar electrodes lose coulombic efficiency as thickness grows
([0046]-[0047], FIGS. 23-24).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-019
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Electrode assembly manufacturing sequence
STATEMENT: >>>
A documented assembly scenario SHALL form iron negative material onto an anode
current collector to create channels, dispose OER into one or more channels, and
assemble ORR with its first surface facing the iron electrode and second surface
in contact with air (EP4602674A1 Claim 86).

Forming MAY include compressing the iron material onto the current collector
(Claim 87) and sintering (Claim 88), followed by adding electrolyte (Claim 89).
DRI pellet beds MAY alternatively be compressed into an anode-current-collector
assembly using passive mechanical locking or threaded rods (US12308414B2
FIGS. 92-93).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
EP4602674A1 Claims 86-89; US12308414B2 FIGS. 92-93. These steps define initial
porosity, contact resistance, and channel geometry states.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-015

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SRS-CHEM
TITLE: Chemistry, electrolyte, and operating conditions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Discharge of the iron electrode in alkaline electrolyte follows Fe + 2OH- <->
Fe(OH)2 + 2e- then further oxidation to magnetite Fe3O4. EP4602674A1 [0042]-[0043]
gives theoretical capacities of 960 mAh/g-Fe for the first step and 320 mAh/g-Fe
for the second, with net volume increase taken up in anode porosity. US12308414B2
states the four-electron air reaction O2 + 2H2O + 4e- -> 4OH- at the ORR triple
phase boundary. Charge reverses iron reduction and evolves oxygen at the OER.
Hydrogen evolution 2H2O + 2e- -> H2 + 2OH- competes with recharge.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-020
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Iron-air reaction set
STATEMENT: >>>
The shared chemistry module SHALL implement:

- Fe + 2OH- <-> Fe(OH)2 + 2e- with 960 mAh/g-Fe theoretical first-step capacity
  (EP4602674A1 [0042]-[0043] Equation 1);
- subsequent oxidation of iron hydroxide to magnetite Fe3O4 with 320 mAh/g-Fe
  theoretical second-step capacity (Equation 2);
- ORR O2 + 2H2O + 4e- -> 4OH- (US12308414B2 detailed description);
- OER 4OH- -> O2 + 2H2O + 4e- as the independent reverse oxygen couple;
- HER 2H2O + 2e- -> H2 + 2OH- as the parasitic charge side reaction
  (EP4602674A1 [0044], [0047]).

Discharge volume increase SHALL be taken up in anode porosity rather than by
inventing extra inventory.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
EP4602674A1 [0042]-[0047]; US12308414B2 air-electrode half-reaction and triple-phase
boundary discussion. Interdigitated OER reduces ionic path length so charge current
is less likely to divert to HER at the electrode front ([0050], FIGS. 19-21).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-021
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Electrolyte composition and pH domain
STATEMENT: >>>
The default liquid electrolyte SHALL be an aqueous alkaline hydroxide solution.

The model SHALL accept compositions disclosed in the patents, including:

- 6 M KOH (US12308414B2; EP4602674A1 simulation electrolyte at 303 K);
- 5.5 M KOH + 0.5 M LiOH;
- 6 M NaOH;
- 5 M NaOH + 1 M KOH;
- about 4 M KOH + 2 M NaOH + 0.05 M LiOH, or 4 M NaOH + 2 M KOH + 0.05 M LiOH;
- high hydroxide at or above 5 M, including 5-6 M, 6-7 M, 7-11 M, 7-10 M,
  7.5-9.5 M, and 7 M or greater (EP4602674A1 electrolyte section).

pH SHALL be modelable as acidic (pH < 4), near-neutral (4 < pH < 10), or alkaline
(pH > 10), with alkaline pH greater than 10 or greater than 12 as preferred
operating points (US12308414B2 electrolyte paragraph).

Electrolyte type MAY also be solid oxide, solid polymer, molten salt, non-aqueous,
gel, or combinations (EP4602674A1 Claims 14-15), but aqueous alkali hydroxide is
the verified modeling default.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 liquid electrolyte examples; EP4602674A1 Claims 14-15 and [0231]-[0241].
High hydroxide is disclosed to increase capacity, improve coulombic efficiency, and
decrease overpotential.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-022
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Temperature, pressure, and oxygen partial pressure
STATEMENT: >>>
Unless a scenario states otherwise, property evaluations SHALL use room temperature
25 C and standard ambient pressure 1 atm as defined in US12308414B2
("room temperature is 25 C"; "standard temperature and pressure is 25 C and
1 atmosphere"). The term "about" SHALL mean a variance of plus or minus 10 percent
or the larger of instrument error, per that patent.

Gas-phase oxygen partial pressure SHALL be parameterizable from 0.01 atm to 100 atm
on discharge and from 0.001 atm to 100 atm on charge, and MAY be raised on
discharge and lowered on charge to increase thermodynamic driving force
(US12308414B2 pressurized-gas paragraph).

EP4602674A1 simulation reference of 6 M KOH at 303 K SHALL be an available
property-model operating point.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 definitions and pO2 operating window; EP4602674A1 FIGS. 19-26
simulation conditions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-023
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Water, carbonation, and hydrogen management
STATEMENT: >>>
The plant SHALL track water inventory changes from ORR/OER, evaporation, and HER.

Carbon dioxide in inlet air SHALL be allowed to carbonate alkaline electrolyte,
changing pH and ionic conductivity and precipitating carbonate that can clog pores
(US12308414B2 CO2 paragraph). A filter/scrubber path MAY circulate electrolyte to
remove CO2 or carbonate.

Floating inert polymer spheres (polypropylene or HDPE, density below the
electrolyte) MAY cover the free electrolyte surface to reduce evaporation and
alkaline misting.

HER and OER bubbles SHALL have egress paths: vertical channels (EP4602674A1
[0056]), separator ribbing ([0048]), 0.1-5 mm iron-OER gaps, and enclosure
ventilation (US12308414B2 lid vent 903).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 water, misting-sphere, CO2, and lid-vent disclosures; EP4602674A1
bubble-egress design of channels and separators.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SRS-MAT
TITLE: Materials, collectors, separators, and safety

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-024
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Electrode and catalyst materials
STATEMENT: >>>
The metal electrode SHALL be selectable as Li, Na, K, Mg, Ca, Si, Al, Zn, or Fe,
or alloys substantially of those elements including FeAl, FeZn, and FeMg, with
iron or iron alloy as the default LODES anode (US12308414B2 anode paragraph).

Anode physical form SHALL include dense or porous solid, mesh, foam, particles,
slurry, ink, suspension, paste, and DRI pellet beds.

ORR gas-diffusion electrodes SHALL support hydrophobic layers with embedded
conductive carbon, PTFE microporous layers, and carbon-fiber layers. Example
loadings include an MPL of about 23 wt% PTFE and 77 wt% carbon black and a first
portion of about 33 wt% PTFE (US12308414B2 cathode construction).

OER electrodes SHALL support porous metal mesh plus oxygen-evolution catalyst
including nickel, Ni-Fe alloys, manganese oxide, iron, NiOx, nickel oxyhydroxide,
iron oxide, and iron oxyhydroxide (EP4602674A1 Claim 11 and catalyst list).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 anode/cathode materials; EP4602674A1 Claim 11 and OER catalyst
paragraph. Dual electrodes allow independent material optimization.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-025
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Current collectors, separators, and seals
STATEMENT: >>>
Anode current collectors SHALL support branch collectors parallel to channels plus
a primary collector or bus bar parallel to the ORR first surface, including bus
bars outside the active-area plane (EP4602674A1 Claims 13, 30-31, 47-48).

Branch collectors SHALL be modelable as highly conductive wires or sheets
(example stainless steel) inside ribs, or as mesh/cage compressing each rib or
anode.

ORR tab current collectors MAY be placed on both faces of the ORR electrode.
ORR seals MAY sandwich a compliant EPDM gasket between a rigid electrode and a
Ni-coated-steel current collector under compressive load (US12308414B2 FIGS. 4B-4C).

Separators SHALL block dissolved oxygen and oxygen bubbles from the anode without
unduly raising ionic resistance, remaining hydrophilic and macroporous
(US12308414B2 FIG. 4A). Separators MAY be compression frames, porous insulators,
ribbed bubble-egress structures, or porous dielectric coatings (EP4602674A1
[0048], Claim 2).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 FIGS. 4A-4C; EP4602674A1 Claims 2, 13, 30-31.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-026
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Hazardous electrolyte containment and electrical isolation
STATEMENT: >>>
Alkaline electrolyte SHALL be treated as a hazardous liquid requiring primary
containment and secondary containment (US12308414B2 vessel discussion).

OER SHALL remain electrically insulated from the iron electrode and from the ORR
electrode except through the intended electrochemical path.

External housing surfaces used for can-negative stacking SHALL have sufficient
insulation for personnel safety while still allowing intended cell-to-cell
contacts (FIG. 11).
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
US12308414B2 containment and can-negative insulation requirements; EP4602674A1
OER electrical isolation statement.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: IA-SYS-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: SEC-SRS-ODE
TITLE: Dynamic modeling rules

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: ODE-based components
STATEMENT: >>>
Every physical component SHALL expose a dynamic ODE model.

Each component SHALL explicitly define: state vector, state units, initial
conditions, input variables, output variables, governing differential equations,
algebraic constitutive relations, physical parameters, boundary conditions,
conservation residuals, numerical constraints, and associated StrictDoc
requirement IDs.

Every component SHALL provide a rhs() method returning state derivatives.

The generic mathematical representation SHALL be:

  dx/dt = f(t, x, inputs, parameters)

Where required:

  0 = g(t, x, algebraic_variables, inputs, parameters)

Algebraic variables SHALL be solved consistently during RHS evaluation or through
a supported DAE backend.

An artificial time constant SHALL NOT be introduced solely to make an instantaneous
physical relation appear dynamic.

Passive structures, such as current collectors, SHALL possess actual dynamic states
where justified, such as temperature. Their instantaneous electrical resistance
SHALL remain an algebraic relation.

Patent-derived algebraic laws SHALL include Ohmic drop, hydraulic orifice and
equalized stacked-ORR pressure drop, Nernst potential, and Faraday mapping of
current to reaction rate.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Every DynamicComponent publishes StateSpec metadata and a deterministic
rhs(t, y, inputs, context). Algebraic electrical resistance is not converted into
a fake lag state.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Shared component models
STATEMENT: >>>
Individual component simulations and the integrated battery SHALL use the same
implementation.

The system SHALL NOT contain separate, simplified physics solely for Jupyter
examples.

Reduced-order versions MAY be implemented, but SHALL be explicitly identified and
tested against the corresponding higher-fidelity models.

Patent architecture options (floating versus submerged ORR, planar versus
interdigitated OER, bifunctional versus dual cathode) SHALL be selected by
configuration flags on the shared components, not by forked governing equations.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Changed because plant notebooks import plant_sim component RHS functions (and
ironair.chemistry), not a second ironair.components physics tree. Reduced-order
models remain named with a reduced_order flag or class name.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: IA-SYS-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Simulation fidelity
STATEMENT: >>>
The software SHALL support lumped ODE models, spatially discretized ODE models,
coupled differential-algebraic models, reduced-order dynamic models, and fully
integrated system simulations.

Spatially distributed PDE formulations SHALL be discretized using finite-volume or
finite-difference methods to produce systems of ODEs or DAEs.

Through-plane ionic gradients in thick iron electrodes and oxygen profiles in GDL
and stacked ORR columns SHALL be representable by spatial discretization when
high-fidelity mode is selected (EP4602674A1 [0046]-[0047]; US12308414B2 stacked
ORR).
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
CoupledSystem accepts lumped and spatially discretized components. Spatial
components document their discretization method and node count.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
